misalignment-17bca134.conceptual_definition:
The formula relates the mass of an axion particle (
$m_a$
) to the energy scale at which a global symmetry is broken (
$f_a$
). This relationship is fundamental in models of axion physics, particularly those addressing the strong CP problem in quantum chromodynamics.

helmholtz-free-energy.conceptual_definition:
The Helmholtz free energy, denoted by 
A
, is a thermodynamic potential that measures the "useful" energy available to a system at a constant temperature (

T
) and volume (

V
). It is defined as the difference between the internal energy (

U
) of the system and the product of its temperature and entropy (

T


S
). This quantity is particularly useful in processes occurring at constant temperature and volume, as the decrease in Helmholtz free energy corresponds to the maximum amount of work that can be extracted from the system.
